const SLOTS = {"nz": {"date": "2026-10-08", "time_nzt": "20:00", "week": 1, "idea_id": "qsme-nz-facebook-group", "title": "Which Dave?", "existing_project": "2026-10-02-qsme-nz-which-dave", "format": "short", "kind": "skit (funny)", "length_s": 30, "aspect": "9:16 (+4:5 Facebook feed crop)", "platforms": ["Instagram Reels", "TikTok", "Facebook Reels", "Facebook feed (4:5)", "YouTube Shorts"], "hook_text": "212 comments. Still no builder.", "concept": "Already produced (2.5s hook plus a 27.5s body). Mel asks the local community page for a builder and gets 212 comments about at least six Daves, until Dave himself turns up asking 'Which Dave do you mean?'. The thread and the joke stay. The product beat must be finished to the fact-check before posting. The reel body, static subline, caption, paid copy and VO were already cleared of 'Licence-verified trades' and 'compared line by line' on 2 Oct; the Figma carousel slide 6 still carries both claims and must be fixed before any export, and any verified-profile placeholder goes too. Also swap the licence setup still in the thread ('Must be licensed' / '…is anyone here licensed?' / 'Dave is.') for '…can anyone actually come and quote?' / 'Dave can.', so the thread doesn't set up a licensing promise QSME can't keep yet. The week-1 rebuild needs no owner recording, so the current owner-recording placeholders (tender send-out and Compare bids table) come out. Hook: the H1 text over the full-frame kinetic thread, with the count jumping 197, 205, 212 (no hand shot); H2 'Which Dave?' is the A/B variant. From 13.5s to 25.5s: 'Or. Put the actual job on QSME.' over the iPhone app still 04-project (demo data), cropped to the tile grid ('Ask for quotes', 'Invite') with the '42 Rimu Street townhouses' header covered, because a seeded street address could match a real home and it isn't Mel's job. Then muted, cropped frames from the tenders walkthrough recreation (scope the package, pull lines from the SOQ; no comparison, no publish-to-market and no 'Quick Jobs' frames) and the contacts recreation (muted; skip any frame saying awarded people are saved to contacts automatically), all labelled 'Recreation of the app · mock data'. Captions: 'Send one job to the trades you choose.' / 'Every one prices the same lines.' Callback payoff: the red-marker tally redraws as 'Dave count: 1 (tick) — the one you invited.' / 'Know which Dave.' End card: 'Free to join. No listing fee on tenders. Your own crew is always free. qsme.co.nz'. Post caption: 'Asked for a builder. Got Dave. Several of him. Got a good Dave? Tag him.' The silent cut ships with captions, and Mel's VO from vo-script.md is added later (update vo04/vo05 to the new captions).", "features": ["Tender cut from an SOQ pocket: private or public, invitations and share link", "Contacts and People (your own crew list)", "QSME iPhone/iPad app (project screen still, demo data)"], "owner_recordings_needed": [], "why_this_slot": "It has to run in week 1 or 2. With the product beat rebuilt from walkthrough recreations and a phone still, it needs no owner recording, so it becomes week 1's funny short. It covers the other half of pre-commit homework: don't pick your builder from a comment thread. Thursday 8pm suits community-group humour, which is Facebook-heavy and peaks on Thursday evenings, when people tag a mate going into the weekend (the time people post 'anyone recommend a builder?'). The repair (Figma slide 6, the licence setup and the recreation-based product beat) must be finished and checked by Wed 7 Oct.", "edition": "nz"}, "global": {"date": "2026-10-06", "time_nzt": "10:30 NZDT (Tue 08:30 Sydney/Melbourne AEDT, 07:30 Brisbane; Mon 22:30 London)", "week": 1, "idea_id": "qsme-build-six-quotes-six-formats", "title": "Six bids. Six formats.", "existing_project": "2026-10-02-qsme-build-six-bids-six-formats", "format": "short", "kind": "kinetic", "length_s": 30, "aspect": "4:5", "platforms": ["LinkedIn (founder profile; QSME page reposts with a one-line comment at 07:30 London the same day)", "YouTube Shorts (9:16 version, still to make from the 4:5 master)"], "hook_text": "6 bids. 6 formats. (chip: 'Tender closed 5:00pm', counter 0/6)", "concept": "The plasterboard & ceilings tender closes at 5:00pm, and six bids land at 4:59 in six formats: a PDF scanned sideways, a spreadsheet that is one merged cell, a lump sum 'as discussed', an email saying 'price below' with nothing below, the cheapest bid (which excludes ceilings on page 9), and a photo of a whiteboard. A deadpan count runs 0/6 → 6/6 and ends in a status flip ('Honestly? Most complete one here.'), then a self-own: 'In fairness… mine said \"drawings attached, please price.\"' The product moment is all labelled 'Illustrative — swap for real QSME screen (demo data)'. 'So we built QSME. Same lines for every bidder.' plays over six identical bidder sheets with the rate column blank ('Bidders never see your rates or budget.'). Then 'Six bids. One table.' over a Compare bids totals table (excl./incl. tax, 'Lowest' on Bidder F at 71,300), then 'Award → contract created' (milestones, retention 5%, 'Next: make the agreement → send for e-sign'). End card: Book a 30-minute demo · qsme.build. Checked 2 Oct: the line × bidder matrix fix is already done. outputs/six-bids-linkedin-4x5.mp4 was re-rendered at 21:10 from the corrected motion source. It has no line × bidder grid and no 'line by line', the whiteboard gap is closed, and QA passed on the 4:5 safe box. It runs 29.8s, and vo-script.md is retimed to it; the Kiwi VO goes in after the ElevenLabs upgrade. The only piece still to make is the 9:16 Shorts version: place the 4:5 master in an r9x16 motion-kit page, scaled to sit inside the 65,300,1015,1250 safe box, and QA it with --check. The illustrative screens stay for week 1 (no owner recordings); Session A footage replaces them only in a later paid cut. Hold the carousel and statics. post.md now says slide 8 is 'Same lines. One table. Award.', but figma-scripts/03-section2-carousel.js still builds 'Same lines. Side by side. Award.', so fix the script before building them.", "features": ["Tender cut from an SOQ pocket: private or public, invitations and share link", "What a bidder sees and how they price (rates and budget never shown)", "Compare bids: totals excluding and including GST, with a 'Lowest' tag", "Award in one click: the winning bid becomes a contract with milestones and retention"], "owner_recordings_needed": [], "why_this_slot": "Opens the month with the highest-scoring idea (18/20). It's already rendered and fact-checked, so week 1 starts with no production risk. It starts the plasterboard & ceilings package (Bid F, 71,300) that 'Why six bids never compare' and 'The Transposition' continue in week 2. Tuesday 08:30 in Sydney/Melbourne is 10:30 in NZ, so the founder's home network seeds comments in the first hour. The post is about 9 hours old, with momentum, when London and the Gulf start work.", "edition": "global"}}
